{"year":"2025","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"The 40th edition took place on February 22, 2025, at the Santa Monica Pier, again hosted by <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1093920, 'screen_type': person}\">Aidy Bryant</a>. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1064213, 'screen_type': movie}\">Anora</a> (2024), by <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 118415, 'screen_type': person}\">Sean Baker</a>, won the awards for feature, director and lead performance, with <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1640439, 'screen_type': person}\">Mikey Madison</a>, while <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1158915, 'screen_type': movie}\">Dìdi</a> (released in Brazil as <i>Caçula</i>), by <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 2602036, 'screen_type': person}\">Sean Wang</a>, won for first feature and first screenplay. The ceremony paid tribute to Josh Welsh, president of Film Independent, who died in December 2024. <i>Television awards are not included.</i>"},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Picture","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":1064213,"name":"Anora","image_path":"/v8Pq2MwPXWDCg1MF3UxNlBCkgDA.jpg","director":"Sean Baker","winner":true},{"type":"movie","id":858017,"name":"I Saw the TV Glow","image_path":"/q01inF0310hkfGL9Z5T6yuneIQI.jpg","director":"Jane Schoenbrun","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":1028196,"name":"Nickel Boys","image_path":"/hlTuZinZ2EvrkTKpW66z2RXySmE.jpg","director":"RaMell Ross","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":1155828,"name":"Sing Sing","image_path":"/3cunENI433NmzwEM0rJIqN4Eypd.jpg","director":"Greg Kwedar","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":933260,"name":"The Substance","image_path":"/vWeOgzlhnP1sS23H3rzctGHB9Nb.jpg","director":"Coralie Fargeat","winner":false}]},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Director","nominee_list":[{"type":"person","id":118415,"name":"Sean Baker","image_path":"/wKfNgfRvPhLHMrwuweSwLOmhRzT.jpg","winner":true,"movie":{"type":"movie","id":1064213,"name":"Anora","image_p